commit d4fa7be1c2fef65ed13a4f73bd58e0a23a0ba307
Author: ahuzmeza <32289581+ahuzmeza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 21:10:09 2026 +0200

    Qwen3-TTS: fix the upsample bias counted twice at chunk joins (#350)
    
    * Qwen3-TTS: count the upsample bias once when streaming decode joins chunks
    
    DecoderBlockUpsample.step carries the transposed conv's last kernel-stride
    outputs into the next chunk and adds them to that chunk's head. Both already
    include the conv bias, so every chunk join got it twice and the audio just
    after each join came out wrong. generateStream joins chunks throughout, and
    generate() decodes in 300-token chunks, so any clip over 24 s has joins too.
    On the 1.7B Base 8-bit model, codes of Tests/media/conversational_a.wav
    decoded in 25-token chunks differed from a full decode by up to 0.66 (SNR 24
    dB); with the fix the largest difference is 1.8e-5 (SNR 111 dB).
    
    The test decodes six frames in full and in three streaming steps with
    nonzero biases and expects the same samples.
    
    * Make STT stream tests independent of scheduler timing
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Lucas Newman <lucasnewman@me.com>

