commit 34ba52c919372905059749f7b030e4c17734efed
Author: ahuzmeza <32289581+ahuzmeza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 29 18:49:34 2026 +0200

    IndexTTS: give the mel sequence the reference's positions (#316)
    
    The start mel token was appended to the text tokens, so it took a text embedding at a text position, and each generated mel token took mel position prompt_length + k. In the reference (index-tts GPT2InferenceModel) the start mel token is a mel embedding at mel position 0. With the prompt's ~35-60 positions added, the GPT began part-way into the utterance and dropped its opening words.
    
    Generated tokens now take mel position k + 2, as in the reference's kv-cache path (its default with fp16 on CUDA). Its CPU/MPS path and its training forward use k + 1; that measures the same here (12/450).
    
    mlx-community/IndexTTS, Tests/media/conversational_a.wav as reference, 10 sentences x 3 runs, Release CLI on a Mac mini M2 Pro, Whisper large-v3-turbo word error rate: 171/450 = 0.380 before (words near the start lost or garbled in every run, e.g. "The bus took the long way around the harbor." for "The bridge was closed for repairs, so the bus took the long way around the harbour.") -> 12/450 = 0.027 after (only "woodsmoke" and numerals). With --temperature 0, one of the sentences comes out as 26 s of near-silence before, the full sentence after.
    
    Tests: the prompt ends with the start mel token's mel embedding at position 0, and the second decode step uses mel position 2; both fail on main.

